// classic-deliv: the reliable broadcast of Birman et al. as LDFI (SIGMOD 2015) §3.1.5 states it: a site that receives
// a message sends a copy to all other sites and delivers it. As the paper describes the Dedalus version, every copy
// received is relayed again, so a failure-free run relays forever ("it has infinite behaviors like the protocols
// submitted in Rounds 2-3"): redundancy in space, but a partial broadcast whose relays are all lost is never repaired.
// Delivery (`log`) happens at the step after receipt. Re-derived from the paper text (derived = true).
// Blossom golden corpus; see ../../README.md.

node(Node, Neighbor)@next :- node(Node, Neighbor);
log(Node, Pload)@next :- log(Node, Pload);

bcast(Other, Pload)@async :- bcast(Site, Pload), node(Site, Other);
log(Site, Pload)@next :- bcast(Site, Pload);
